schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "Grafana gives two minor releases' advance notice before removing a deprecated feature"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Grafana's writers' toolkit distinguishes deprecation ("planned for
    removal in a future release") from removal ("removed and no longer
    supported"), and the team notifies users two minor releases in advance
    before a deprecated feature is actually removed.
  evidence: >-
    Cited in the article from Grafana Writers' Toolkit's "Deprecate or remove
    content" page (grafana.com/docs/writers-toolkit/write/deprecate-remove/),
    listed in the article's References.
  interpretation: >-
    Used as the model timeline the article recommends porting into a
    commons's own deprecation banners: leave the page live, warn readers, and
    give a real interval before anything disappears.
  uncertainty: >-
    Reproduces Grafana's own published policy as stated in the article's
    citation; not independently re-verified against Grafana's live docs for
    this ingestion.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/archive-compost.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-d6e9e6e15257
  source_lineage: archive-compost.md
